{
  "mappings": {
    "_meta": {
      "no_date_field": [
        "NO date-typed field belongs in this mapping, ever.",
        "These rows exist so the Overview verdict cards cannot be re-scoped by the dashboard",
        "time picker. Kibana applies the dashboard range to an ES|QL card by filtering on the",
        "index's date field; with none, the picker cannot reach these rows at all. Verified in",
        "the browser 2026-09-05 (kibana/probe_notime.py): at Last 15 minutes a card reading a",
        "no-date index returned every row while a control on workout-sessions returned zero.",
        "Adding a date field here - even one called computed_at - silently reverts the whole",
        "mechanism with no visible symptom. computed_through is a keyword for that reason.",
        "date_detection is off and dynamic is strict for the same reason. The guard above reads this file, but Elasticsearch maps what it is SENT: an unmapped field holding '2026-10-24' would be auto-detected as a date and revert the mechanism with nothing in the repo to show for it. Strict makes the unmapped field a rejected document at index time instead - loud, in CI, before it can lie."
      ],
      "written_by": "ingest/derive.py signal_docs()"
    },
    "dynamic": "strict",
    "date_detection": false,
